# CODEOWNERS — automatic review routing.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the matching owner when a PR touches these
# paths. The LAST matching pattern wins, so the catch-all is first and the
# specific paths override it.
#
# Pairs with branch protection's "Require review from Code Owners" (KAN-2).
# That box is NOT ticked yet — until it is, these are suggestions, not gates.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A pattern that matches nothing is worse than no pattern.
#
# It reads as coverage and provides none, and GitHub says nothing about it —
# a rule for a path that no longer exists simply never fires. Five auth paths
# in this file went that way when `identity` moved into `src/modules/`
# (ADR 0003): the security-review routing looked intact and had silently
# stopped applying to every file it named.
#
# `platform/src/__tests__/architecture/codeowners.test.ts` now fails the build
# when a pattern here resolves to nothing, so the next move cannot repeat it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACTION REQUIRED: per-area owners still route to one person.
#
# Repo collaborators are @makuachteny, @senyomd and @ikyalo01. Every path below
# is mapped so review routing actually works, but they all point at
# @makuachteny because who owns which subsystem was never recorded — and
# naming someone a required reviewer is a commitment on their behalf, not a
# formatting detail.
#
# To spread the load, change the handle on the right of any line. The two
# reassignments that were previously pencilled in here were:
#     /mobile/     -> @ikyalo01
#     /website/    -> @senyomd
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                           @makuachteny

# --- Application code ------------------------------------------------------
/platform/                  @makuachteny
/mobile/                    @makuachteny
/website/                   @makuachteny

# --- Domain modules --------------------------------------------------------
# One entry per module, so ownership follows the boundary rather than a list of
# scattered files that goes stale the moment anything moves. A module is a
# reviewable unit: its public surface is one file, and everything behind that
# surface belongs to whoever owns the domain.
#
# Add a line here when a domain lands. Ordering within this block does not
# matter — the modules do not overlap, which is the point of them.
/platform/src/modules/identity/       @makuachteny
/platform/src/modules/communication/  @makuachteny
/platform/src/modules/analytics/      @makuachteny
/platform/src/modules/feature-catalog/ @makuachteny

# --- Data & sync -----------------------------------------------------------
# Patient data, CouchDB→Postgres projection and the offline sync engine.
# Changes here can silently corrupt or drop PHI — keep a second pair of eyes.
/sync-worker/                    @makuachteny
/platform/src/modules/analytics/api/  @makuachteny
/platform/src/lib/db/            @makuachteny
/platform/src/lib/db.ts          @makuachteny
/platform/src/lib/sync/          @makuachteny

# --- Security-sensitive paths ----------------------------------------------
# Auth, proxy (Next 16's middleware), CSRF and token handling. Listed AFTER the
# application-code and module blocks on purpose: last match wins, so these
# override /platform/ and /platform/src/modules/identity/ and keep auth changes
# routed to security review.
#
# The identity module's `core/` and `policy/` directories are where the
# credentials live — sessions, tokens, CSRF, the request-time guard, the
# password rules. They are the reason this block exists; the rest of the module
# is ordinary domain code covered above.
/platform/src/proxy.ts                          @makuachteny
/platform/src/modules/identity/core/            @makuachteny
/platform/src/modules/identity/policy/          @makuachteny
/platform/src/modules/identity/provisioning/    @makuachteny
/platform/src/modules/tenancy/                 @makuachteny
/platform/src/lib/field-encryption.ts           @makuachteny
/platform/src/lib/config-validation.ts          @makuachteny
/fingerprint-bridge/                            @makuachteny

# --- Architecture boundaries -----------------------------------------------
# The rules that keep the modules apart, and the tests that prove they hold.
# A change here changes what the whole codebase is allowed to do.
/docs/adr/                                          @makuachteny
/platform/eslint.config.mjs                         @makuachteny
/platform/src/__tests__/architecture/               @makuachteny

# --- Infrastructure, CI/CD and deploy --------------------------------------
# A bad change here can take down staging/production or leak secrets.
/.github/                   @makuachteny
/infra/                     @makuachteny
/scripts/                   @makuachteny
/docker-compose.yml         @makuachteny
/docker-compose.ghcr.yml    @makuachteny
/deploy.sh                  @makuachteny

# --- Repo-root tooling -----------------------------------------------------
/package.json               @makuachteny
/.lintstagedrc.mjs          @makuachteny
/.husky/                    @makuachteny
/.nvmrc                     @makuachteny
